# C32 remediation after attempt-01 (8/6/7/7/7, fail)

| Finding | Remediation | Where |
|---|---|---|
| R1 no authoritative read/write classification or native branch | `HarnessApproval.effect` (`readOnly` / `mayChange`) is set by the core: desktop reads and commands in a read-only project are read-only; file changes, commands with changes allowed and every workspace MCP tool may change things. Allowing a `mayChange` decision opens the native confirmation (`Effect::ConfirmHarness`); only its private completion sends the allow; refused, the decision stays pending; a confirmation whose decision is gone is dismissed (`retire_harness_confirmation`). The page shows the effect truthfully ("Read-only" / "May change things", "Approve once" / "Approve…"). Tests: `harness_tools::reads_are_decided_in_the_page_and_changes_need_the_native_confirmation` (read declined: nothing read; write command: sheet refused, nothing runs; accepted, it runs once); component "says when a decision may change things"; native C32-N02 (Approve… opens the sheet, Cancel runs nothing, Allow once runs it) | `harness.rs`, `session.rs`, `harness_tools.rs`, `authority.rs`, `harness.tsx` |
| R2 first-send continuation | The queued first message is bound to the start receipt's operation (and to the conversation it replaces); the box keeps the text until `sendHarness` is admitted; a refused start, a failed startup or another conversation drops the queue with an explanation and nothing is sent elsewhere; a refused send leaves the text in the new conversation's box. Test: "keeps the first message until a conversation takes it" | `harness.tsx` |
| R3 new investigation | "New investigation" (and the contextual "Start a new investigation") switch the composer to the next conversation while one runs; sending ends the current one (its transcript kept), clears it and starts a new one, which alone receives the message; a pending decision holds it back. Tests: "a new investigation while one runs…", "a pending decision holds a new investigation back" | `harness.tsx` |
| R4 unsent and sign-in failure; decline label | A message the core gives back returns to its conversation's box with the sign-in failure text and "Nothing was resent"; the write-renewal decline is "Not now", explaining that nothing is sent and the folder access stays as chosen. Test: "returns an unsent message to the box…" | `harness.tsx`, `copy.ts` |
| R5 outcomes and saved claims | The C19–C22 texts are reused: a failed conversation, a stopped, cut, failed or refused answer, a failed cleanup each have a distinct status (alert or status with an icon word); entry states (in progress, stopped, cut, failed, declined) are labelled; the saved line comes only from `savedAt`/`saveFailure`. Test: "shows how the conversation stands…" | `harness.tsx` |
| R6 drafts | Drafts live in the shell store by tenant, workspace and conversation (`harnessDrafts`): kept across navigation and a tenant round trip, never shared, never sent by themselves. Test: "keeps each draft in its tenant, workspace and conversation…" | `store.ts`, `harness.tsx` |
| R7 the mcp lifecycle's read | A desktop read tool `mcpServers` reads the conversation workspace's MCP catalog (`GatewayRead::McpServers`), decided in the page; all three lifecycles now read through desktop tools (search, mcpServers, API key inventory); the mcp recommendation describes the pii-check guardrail it proposes. Tests: `harness_tools::the_mcp_catalog_is_read_for_the_engine_only_once_the_operator_allows_it`; component V2-T17 per lifecycle; native C32-N03 | `tools.rs`, `harness_tools.rs`, fixtures |
| Optional | C32-N03 now requires `apply_gated` and `engine_gone`; follow-ups of an ended conversation are no longer actionable and say so | `acceptance_c32.py`, `harness.tsx` |

A call that can no longer run (a workspace MCP tool whose server sign-in lapsed) is still declined at once, without a sheet, as before C32. The shared Harness test desk accepts the native sheet the way an operator would (`harness_process/desk.rs`); tests of the sheet itself set their own answer.

Provenance P44–P49 record the deviations (P48: desktop reads now ask; P49: the native branch C27 assumed existed is implemented). The stopped-turn Harness test's slow read was widened (3 s → 6 s) so the stop lands first under the full suite's load.

B1/E1 (the C29 live Vulture verification receipt) stay owner-gated (`evidence/C29/live-scope-request.md`).
